  "segments": [
    {
      "text": "Um, lately, I've been looking around my living room and, like, feeling like it's missing something. Everything works fine. The tap isn't leaking. The lights are bright. The couch is comfy. But, you know, it still feels a bit cold, almost like I'm living in someone else's space. I'll be scrolling through my phone and see these cozy rugs, big leafy plants, and oh, those cool prints people put on their walls. I mean, I start imagining how much warmer the place would look with a few of those touches. Then I check the price and go, \"Well, maybe not right now.\" It's that tug between wanting it to feel like my home and basically wanting to keep my savings intact. My friends say, \"Oh, but why don't you just buy one thing at a time? It'll add up before you know it.\" And I'm sitting there thinking, \"So do I start with a lamp or a plant? Do I wait for a sale?\" I'm actually kind of indecisive about it. The house is totally functional, and I'm grateful for that. But I crave that feeling when you walk in and everything, uh, reflects your style. Maybe I'll pick up a small plant soon and, well, slowly build from there. There's no rush to make it perfect, right?",
      "start_time": 0.119,
      "end_time": 81.759,
